3 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483283 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483283 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483283 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483283 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6f364f54-37f9-5c16-b23e-1b97b8dd9c4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1071 "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $35\\,832\\,4◻2$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $6$\n\nII. $7$\n\nIII. $9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb148c29-2fa3-5a15-9be6-3a95df07f188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483402 #edb/ref 1074 "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n3+5+8+3+2+4+◻+2=27+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $6$ into the blank, we get $35\\,832\\,462,$ which is divisible by $2.$ Then the sum of the digits is $27+6=33,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\n- If we substitute $7$ into the blank, we get $35\\,832\\,472,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $27+7=34,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $9$ into the blank, we get $35\\,832\\,492,$ which is divisible by $2.$ Then the sum of the digits is $27+9=36,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132400" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1071 "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $11\\,521\\,6◻6$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $3$\n\nII. $7$\n\nIII. $9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4adaad6-9b04-5b58-a83e-194edc0437bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483410 #edb/ref 1074 "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n1+1+5+2+1+6+◻+6=22+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $3$ into the blank, we get $11\\,521\\,636,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $22+3=25,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $7$ into the blank, we get $11\\,521\\,676,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $22+7=29,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $9$ into the blank, we get $11\\,521\\,696,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $22+9=31,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483449 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186483467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483449 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d9e737d-3beb-558d-b409-89e4144e50cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483449 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186483402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483467 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186483503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483467 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d652c62-b3a3-5b32-af56-3ba9c69395ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483467 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186483410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483503 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e6219abf-feda-5f67-92ad-2d82ceb7152e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483503 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172311 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
